  ("Traumatic or degenerative tear", "<p>A traumatic tear appears after a twist with the foot planted, often during sport, and may come with ligament injuries. A degenerative tear appears without a clear injury, through wear, and often coexists with early osteoarthritis. Degenerative tears are frequently seen on the MRI scans of people over 40 who have no pain, so the image is always interpreted together with the examination.</p>"),
